"79_writestream_new.mst — MACDART: WriteStream>>new initializes its backing.

 18_writestream.mst's WriteStream keeps a `collection`/`position` pair and is
 created with `WriteStream on: String new`, but it never defines a class-side
 `new`. So a bare `WriteStream new` fell to the inherited basicNew with nil ivars,
 and the first nextPut:/nextPutAll: did arithmetic on a nil position (`+` on nil).
 A default `new` should just stream onto an empty String — the ANSI/Squeak
 behaviour — so `anArray printOn: WriteStream new` and friends work. Loads after
 18 (file 79); reopen adds the missing constructor."

WriteStream class >> new [ ^self on: String new ]

"next: n put: anObject — write n copies of anObject (ANSI/Squeak). The one
 WriteStream method a sweep found missing next to nextPut:/nextPutAll:."
WriteStream >> next: anInteger put: anObject [
    anInteger timesRepeat: [ self nextPut: anObject ].
    ^anObject
]
